From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:05:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(kanban): mint ordered ids in legacy-cursor test [daveey]

test_legacy_rows_do_not_advance_policy_cursor assumed every legacy id
sorts after every policy id. Synced task ids are a 48-bit millisecond
prefix plus 16 random bits, so ids minted in the same millisecond order
randomly: CI run 43198984703 minted the last policy id and the first
legacy id in ms 0x01a1cf492085 and the assertion failed
('...57d' > '...8311'). Mint sequential ids for this test so the
precondition holds by construction.

With the clock frozen to one millisecond, the old test fails 39/40 and
the new one passes 40/40.
---
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_recovery_routing.py | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_recovery_routing.py b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_recovery_routing.py
index fd954f5258..ef536a1c9f 100644
--- a/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_recovery_routing.py
+++ b/tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_recovery_routing.py
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 """Recovery and renewal retain independent routing and diagnostic ownership."""
+import itertools
 import json
 
 from hermes_cli import kanban_db_sync as sync
@@ -12,8 +13,12 @@ conn = fixtures.conn
 setup = fixtures.setup
 
 
-def test_legacy_rows_do_not_advance_policy_cursor(setup):
+def test_legacy_rows_do_not_advance_policy_cursor(setup, monkeypatch):
     db, hub = setup
+    # Synced ids order by their millisecond prefix only; ids minted in the same
+    # millisecond order by random bits, so mint them in creation order here.
+    minted = itertools.count(1)
+    monkeypatch.setattr(sync, "new_task_id", lambda _conn: f"t_{next(minted):016x}")
     policy = [reserve.acknowledged(db) for _ in range(wp.MAX_RESERVES_PER_TICK + 1)]
     legacy = [fixtures.make(db) for _ in range(wp.MAX_RESERVES_PER_TICK)]
     assert min(legacy) > max(policy)
